A||||15||batboy||computer case modding craze||||6||
Z||000000||batboy||01-15-2001||03:36 PM||||First off, I'm normally a mature guy. But somehow, I got caught up in this big case modding craze. Computer overclockers and hardware geeks have started "ricing" out their computers nowadays in a brand new fad.<P>My old generic ATX mid-tower case is very functional and has served me well for a couple years now. Is it so bad that I want an unique, individualized, and attractive case with improved cooling, too?<P>I wanted my mods to be conservatively and tastefully done. You know, a classic work of art, not a "low rider" of the computer world like some I've seen. Neon and bright flash... forget it. Oh yeah, most important, has to be real cheap too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I have a total of 4 auxilary case fans, 2 pulling fresh air in and two exhausting warm air out. One is a slot fan right next to the video card. I'm using some black plastic auto wiring loom conduit and small wire ties to round my flat ribbon cables so that they don't block air flow as much.<P>I decided that adding a noisy "blowhole" fan in the top wasn't critical with my setup, but I still didn't want hot air to build up in the top area. So. I drilled a small pattern of holes in the top of my case to allow more ventilation.<P>off to Wal-Mart I go, where I bought a couple cans of Fleck Stone spray can paint. This is a slightly textured base paint with little splatters of other colors mixed in. I chose a gray color (several to choose from) that turned out quite excellent. It looks just like granite rock. Nice! You have to spray about three light coats to cover it good. Of course the proper sanding and prep before hand needs to be done.<P>I'm posting a pic of how it looks. The front face plate is not done yet. I'm still deciding if I should just trim it or paint it granite too. Wow, this is fun! You're only limited by your imagination. Lastly, I'll probably add some little bat sticker onto the front in honor of my nickname.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/comp-granite1.jpg">  <P>Here's a closer look to show off the paint job a little better and to let you have a look at my drilled top vent.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/comp-granite-top.jpg">  <P>Get busy people, too cold to mod the Fiero, so mod your computer. Someone HAS to do the classic hotrodder flames and pin stripes.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 01-15-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||pHoOl||01-15-2001||04:17 PM||||This is funny, cause i just added twin 4.5 inch fans.  haven't thought about drilling holes yet as the computer was just built by me a few months ago.  No need to overclock yet.  That granite does look cool though, you'll have to tell me where you got it.  And i was thinking if i got my hands on an air brush, i would paint one of the filler plates on the front with my nickname.  I guess i'm just a computer geek at heart too.  Can't mod the fiero, so i guess i'll have to mod the computer.  oh yeah, and litestep is my friend.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: phool88fiero<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/pHoOl_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||01-15-2001||04:38 PM||||I have been thinking of stenciling <B><I>DELL</B></I> diagonally across both sides of my case but I know for sure that Im going to throw some low profile casters on my computer desk.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Songman||01-15-2001||05:15 PM||||You guys are lucky! I have so much stuff added into my computer that I can't even put the case on... I guess it all depends on how you feel about the look of duct tape holding the extra hard drives in!<P>Filled up all my IDE slots so had to go SCSI and now have hard drives and other peripherals stacked on top of the case! It's tough running a server and having to have all that space!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-15-2001||05:37 PM||||Actually, my computer-case has an "over-the-hood-scoop".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>It also has a few extra switches here and there, mainly to switch on extra fans. But, although it's a C566 overclocked to 850, it doesn't need any extra cooling. It's rock stable with the standard CPU-cooler.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||batboy||01-15-2001||05:38 PM||||pH, I got that paint at Wal-Mart, other colors to choose from too. Also, you need to top it off with a clear coat. I've seen pics of several cases that have graphics air brushed on the sides of the case. Another popular trick is to cut out a window in the side and install a plexiglass window. Then they put neon lights inside. Lots of different ways to add extra cooling fans...the sign of an overclocker.<P>My rig is: Abit SE6 mobo, Celeron 566 overclocked to 850 MHz, 256 meg PC133 RAM, etc. I can clock it at 950, but nothing above that is stable. I'm in the process of trading in my Golden Orb cooler for a new Alpha PAL6035 with a thermistor controlled fan. After I improve the cooling, I'm going to throw more voltage to the CPU core. This chip WILL run at 1+ GHz. It's do or die...if it fries, I'm buying a new P-III chip. I wanna dance at the 1 Gig. party!||||reg||1
